      "candidate_id": "c2",
      "decision": "uncertain",
      "effect": "unclear",
      "reason": "gzclose_r provably returns early on non-read handles, and the harness then nulls the handle. But a witness that hits case 21 must open with the one-character mode \"w\": the two op bytes are mode[0] and the next input byte. No supplied evidence shows that gz_open accepts \"w\" and returns a write-mode state. The library test only shows that \"wb\" succeeds.",
      "finite_witness": "Bytes 02 77 15. mode_sz=2, so mode=\"w\" and data is not advanced. Op 1 is 'w'%26=15 (gzdirect). Op 2 is 0x15=21, which calls gzclose_r and then sets file=NULL. This assumes gzopen(\"w\") returns a write-mode handle.",
      "scope_contract": {
        "status": "established",
        "reason": "Opening, closing and gzclose_r are operations of the harness.",
        "evidence": [
